-- title:
--   Power series vanishing below degree k lie in (X)^k
-- statement:
--   Let $\sigma$ be a finite type and $R$ a commutative ring, let $k$ be a natural number, and let $\varphi$ be a formal power series in the variables indexed by $\sigma$ with coefficients in $R$, i.e. an element of `MvPowerSeries σ R`. Assume that for every exponent vector $m : \sigma \to_{f} \mathbb{N}$ whose degree $m.\mathrm{degree}$ (the sum of its values, i.e. the total degree of the corresponding monomial) is strictly less than $k$, the coefficient of $\varphi$ at $m$ vanishes. The conclusion is that $\varphi$ belongs to the $k$-th power of the ideal of `MvPowerSeries σ R` generated by the set of variables, namely $\big(\mathrm{Ideal.span}\,\{X_i : i \in \sigma\}\big)^k$. Thus a power series all of whose homogeneous components of total degree below $k$ vanish lies in the $k$-th power of the ideal generated by the variables; in particular, for $k = 0$ the assertion is trivial, and the finiteness of $\sigma$ is needed for the statement as given.
--
--   This is the basic estimate underlying $(X)$-adic approximation arguments in power series rings over a commutative ring, relating the vanishing of low-degree coefficients to membership in powers of the ideal of variables. It is used throughout the parts of the formalisation that handle presentations of algebras by power series rings and approximation of maps out of $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$, for instance in the analysis of cotangent complexes of algebra maps and in the patching arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_mem_pow_span_X_of_coeff_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Inverse
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Noetherian

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v w

theorem MvPowerSeries.mem_pow_span_X_of_coeff_eq_zero {σ : Type u} {R : Type v} [Finite σ] [CommRing R] (k : ℕ) (φ : MvPowerSeries σ R) (hφ : ∀ m : σ →₀ ℕ, m.degree < k → MvPowerSeries.coeff m φ = 0) : φ ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : σ → MvPowerSeries σ R)) ^ k := by sorry
